# Cache headers for the deployed bundle.
#
# **Cloudflare Pages appends the values of every rule that matches a request.**
# It does not let a later, more specific rule replace an earlier one. The
# previous version of this file assumed the opposite — a blanket `immutable`
# rule first, then `no-cache` overrides for the entry points — and the result
# was measurable on the live site:
#
#     /index.html   ->  public, max-age=31536000, immutable, no-cache
#     /             ->  public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# Both rules concatenated on the first, which is a contradiction browsers are
# free to resolve either way. The second line is the one that did the damage:
# `/` never matched the `/index.html` rule at all, so the bare URL everybody
# actually visits was cached as immutable for a year. The browser stopped
# asking for the document, never learned a new build existed, and went on
# serving the first deploy indefinitely — while every per-deployment URL
# (`<id>.depcontrol.pages.dev`) looked correct, because a new origin has an
# empty cache.
#
# So: **one rule, no overlaps.** Nothing here can contradict anything else,
# and there is no path that falls through the gap `/` fell through.
#
# `no-cache` is not `no-store`. The browser still keeps every asset; it just
# asks whether its copy is current before using it, and gets a 304 with no body
# when it is. That costs one conditional request per asset per load and buys
# deploys that actually reach people — which the year-long `immutable` did not,
# for anyone who had loaded the site once.
#
# Nothing in a Flutter web bundle is content-hashed — `main.dart.js`,
# `flutter_bootstrap.js` and everything under `assets/` keep their names across
# builds — so there is no file here that `immutable` would be honest about.
# `canvaskit/` is the one arguable exception, and one rule that cannot go wrong
# is worth more than a few saved 304s on it.
#
# Anything in frontend/web/ is copied verbatim into build/web/ by
# `flutter build web`, which is how this reaches the deployed bundle.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
